# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and check it out as LF on
# every platform. Without this, a Windows clone with the default
# `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites line endings on checkout, so the same file
# reads as modified on one machine and clean on another — and the JSONata test
# suite's 1,347 fixture files would each churn.
#
# The suite fixtures are deliberately included: they are JSON and Markdown that
# the runner parses (never byte-compares), so storing them LF-only is both safe
# and what keeps `git status` clean across platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf
